  "label": "User projected onto the drag performer as the subject of the self-acceptance struggle",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the drag performer (visual material) as the embodiment of 'they' in the text, which refers to individuals struggling with self-acceptance. The user identifies with the performer's external confidence (visual) and internal conflict (textual), creating a personal identification with the subject of the message. The drag performer is the focal point of the projection, as the text explicitly addresses 'they' and the visual material directly represents this 'they'.",
